Z||000000||hutch84fierose||07-01-2001||12:44 PM||||The dash in my fiero is a little worn like a lot of people well i found one a guy is gonna sell me for a really good price mint condition........The only question i have what are the step to taking the old one out and puting a new one back in does the windsheild have to be removed???????/HOPE NOT<BR>thank||||reg||6
Z||000001||PBJ||07-01-2001||01:02 PM||||STEPS<P>hood release <BR>steering column cover<BR>speaker grills and speakers<BR>i/p attaching screws<BR>i/p service cover<BR>loosen shoft trim plate<BR>front console tirm plate<BR>front console pad asm<BR>i/p to reinforcemnt screws<BR>i/p pad assembly<P>I hope this helps.  the pictures are a wonderful thing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-01-2001||04:05 PM||||That's soemthign else I did... LOL<BR>You need to take off the 3 screws on the hood release.<BR>Take off the bottom cover for the steering column, 4 small bolts. <BR>Take of the heater vent cover and the center shifter plate.  Remove the gray heater console cover.<BR>It is VERY helpful to drop the steering column, 4 bolts.<BR>I also had my gauge cluster out when I did this which makes it easier too.<BR>Pop off the speaker covers. Take out the speakers and disconenct the wires. There are 2 bolts under each cover that bold foward, they hold inthe top of the dash..<BR>Then in each bottom corner of the dash there is one bolt near the doors. If I rememebr right they were 10mm, but I'm not positive.<BR>Then it should just pop out.<BR>I THINK I covered everything...||||reg||1
